.TH DAYTONA-SESSION 1 "November 2026" "Daytona 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
daytona-session \- start a Daytona desktop session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B daytona-session
[\fIlabwc options\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B daytona-session
starts labwc with Daytona's configuration (NT key bindings, window menu and
theme), which starts \fBdaytona-shell\fR(1). Login managers run it for the
"Daytona" session. It sets, for the session only, \fBGTK_THEME=Daytona\fR,
\fBXCURSOR_THEME\fR to the Chicago95 cursors and \fBQT_STYLE_OVERRIDE=daytona\fR,
so GTK 3 and Qt 6 applications take the NT look.
Further arguments are passed to labwc.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR daytona-shell (1),
.BR labwc (1)
